    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_3",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "The main representatives of the new style, often referred to as ars nova as opposed to the ars antiqua, were the composers Philippe de Vitry and Guillaume de Machaut. In Italy, where the Provençal troubadours had also found refuge, the corresponding period goes under the name of trecento, and the leading composers were Giovanni da Cascia, Jacopo da Bologna and Francesco Landini. Prominent reformer of Orthodox Church music from the first half of 14th century was John Kukuzelis; he also introduced a system of notation widely used in the Balkans in the following centuries.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999918646272,
      "temperature": 0.9999999918646272,
      "expanded": false,
      "visit_count": 0,
